## Fall Ombre Nail Troubleshooting: Common Fixes

Most <strong>fall ombre nails</strong> problems trace back to one of three habits: too much product loaded at once, working too fast between layers, or skipping the practice nail. Slowing down fixes more of this than any product swap does.

If your colours are muddying together, especially mixing warm and cool fall tones, that's a colour family mismatch rather than a technique failure, go back to the pairings above and stay within one temperature. If the sponge leaves a harsh line instead of a fade, you're loading too much colour per dab; wipe the sponge down to nearly nothing and try again with lighter pressure. For gel that smears on cure, the layer went under the lamp before the blend was actually finished. And if someone asks "wait, did you go to a salon?", that's usually the sign the practice-nail habit paid off, your fingers learn the rhythm of dab pressure faster than you'd expect, often within two or three nails on the same hand.

