## How Long Do Fall Ombre Nails Last?

A <strong>fall ombre nails</strong> gel manicure lasts roughly two to three weeks with a proper cure between layers and a sealed top coat. Regular polish holds up for about five to seven days before the tip colour starts showing wear first, since that's the area that takes the most daily contact.

Darker fall pigments, burgundy and espresso especially, tend to show chipping less obviously than a pale pastel would, simply because the colour contrast against bare nail is less stark. That said, cuticle oil nightly and gloves for anything abrasive, washing dishes, gardening, extend either formula noticeably. If you're deciding between the two methods purely on longevity, gel is the better bet for anyone wearing the fade past the two-week mark; regular polish is the faster, lower-commitment option if you're testing a colour combination before deciding whether it's a repeat.

