## Your Fade, Done Properly

A clean fall ombre was never about a special product or a salon-only skill. It was about layering thin, dabbing instead of dragging, and giving dark pigments the extra passes they need to fade instead of smear. Once your fingers learn that rhythm, the fifteen-minute bruise stage stops happening altogether, and what's left is a burgundy-to-rust or mocha-to-caramel gradient that looks considerably more deliberate than the attempt that came before it. Pick one combination from the pairings above, set up a practice nail, and commit to the dab. That's genuinely the whole method.
